[1mOne real translation bug, fixed:[22m the Rust program exited 0 where the C died from [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m. Rust's standard library sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so [38;5;10mwriteln![0m returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m and the code's [38;5;10mlet _ = ...[0m swallowed it. The C keeps the default disposition and is killed with signal 13 on the first [38;5;10mprintf[0m to a closed stdout. Fixed by resetting the disposition to [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m in [38;5;10mmain[0m. I also matched glibc's 4096-byte stdout buffer ([38;5;10mst_blksize[0m, not [38;5;10mBUFSIZ[0m) instead of Rust's 8192 default, so the [38;5;10mwrite()[0m boundaries — and therefore the bytes that escape before that death — line up.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mEverything else already matched[22m, including the parts that look like bugs. Worth knowing about this program: glibc's [38;5;10m%d[0m converts through a [38;5;10mlong[0m accumulator that saturates, then truncates to [38;5;10mint[0m, so [38;5;10m4294967297[0m becomes [38;5;10mx = 1[0m and prints one line, [38;5;10m-4294967293[0m becomes [38;5;10m3[0m, and [38;5;10m99999999999999999999[0m becomes [38;5;10m-1[0m and prints nothing. The Rust already did the same two-step. [38;5;10m-2147483649[0m truncates to [38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m, which is the largest count the loop takes.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe [38;5;10mj += 2[0m overflow is real and I verified it directly.[22m [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m sets no build type, so the C is unoptimized — the disassembly is a plain [38;5;10maddl $0x2[0m on a 32-bit stack slot, which wraps. Reaching it takes ~1.07e9 iterations, so the test streams both programs concurrently and compares byte-for-byte through the wrap; at the analytically predicted offset both emit [38;5;10m1073741824 -2147483648[0m. That test runs ~90–130s and is not [38;5;10m#[ignore][0md.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two harness defects were mine, not the translation's: buffering the [38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m case aborted the test binary with an 8 GiB allocation failure (now a bounded 1 MiB prefix comparison), and a [38;5;10mwindows()[0m marker scan over 23 GB made plain [38;5;10mcargo test[0m take 9m40s (now a closed-form offset, self-checked against a brute-force count).[0m[0m
